FAQ

Q: What are semiconductor filters?

A: Semiconductor filters are specialized filtration products used to remove particles and contaminants from gases, chemicals and liquids used in semiconductor manufacturing.

Q: Where are semiconductor filters used?

A: They are used in wafer fabrication, chemical delivery, gas distribution, cleaning and other semiconductor processing applications.

Q: What drives demand?

A: Demand is supported by advanced manufacturing, tighter contamination control requirements and increasing use of high-purity process materials.

